 #### `pocket_tts` (default)
@@ -127,8 +135,34 @@ say --voice '?'
 
 The short name (e.g. `Samantha`, `Daniel`, `Karen`) is used in API requests. Voice names are case-insensitive; full identifiers (e.g. `com.apple.voice.enhanced.en-US.Samantha`) also work.
 
-> **Note:** Siri voices are not accessible via public AVFoundation APIs and will not appear in the voice list.
-> Personal Voice support (macOS 14+) is planned — see issue #13.
+Siri voices are not accessible through this public `avspeech` engine. Use the
+separate private `siri` engine below for already-installed Siri assets.
+
+#### `siri` — installed natural/neural Siri assets (private API)
+
+Uses Apple's private `SiriTTSService.framework` with local UAF/Gryphon assets.
+The server validates the expected Objective-C ABI, loads the best installed
+voice, and completes a real synthesis at startup; an incompatible macOS update
+therefore fails before the server begins accepting requests.
+
+```yaml
+tts:
+  engine: siri
+  siri:
+    # Optional; omit to prefer a natural voice for the current locale.
+    default_voice: com.apple.siri.tts.voice.en_US.nora.natural.premium
+    max_loaded_voices: 4
+    max_concurrent_syntheses: 4
+    max_queued_requests: 20
+```
+
+Private engines are large and unsafe to tear down, so one serial lane is kept
+resident per used voice and at most four different voices may be loaded in one
+process. A fifth voice returns a restart-required capacity error. This engine
+only scans installed assets and never triggers a private download.
+
+> **Warning:** this is an undocumented Apple API. ABI validation reduces the
+> failure surface but does not make it supported or stable across macOS updates.
 
