-| `response_format` | String | No       | `wav` (default) or `pcm`                           |
+| `response_format` | String | No       | `wav` (default), `pcm`, `opus`, or `aac`            |
 | `speed`           | Double | No       | Playback speed, 0.25-4.0 (default: 1.0)           |
 
-The response is **streamed**: audio begins arriving before synthesis is complete, sentence by sentence. WAV responses include a standard 44-byte header (with unknown-size placeholders) followed by 16-bit PCM; PCM responses are raw 16-bit bytes. The sample rate depends on the active TTS engine (24 kHz for `pocket_tts` and `kokoro`, 22050 Hz for `avspeech`).
+WAV and raw PCM responses are streamed sentence by sentence. `opus` is a
+complete 48 kHz mono RFC 7845 Ogg Opus file targeting 48 kbps constrained VBR;
+`aac` is a complete 48 kHz mono AAC-LC file targeting 64 kbps in an M4A/MP4
+container. Compressed output is completed before response headers are sent so
+an encoder failure remains a normal JSON error. Native PCM sample rate is 24
+kHz for `pocket_tts` and `kokoro`, 22050 Hz for `avspeech`, and 48 kHz for
+`siri`.
 
 Example:
 
@@ -368,6 +408,10 @@ curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/v1/audio/speech \
 
 For the `avspeech` engine, `voice` accepts a display name (case-insensitive, e.g. `Samantha`) or a full identifier (e.g. `com.apple.voice.enhanced.en-US.Samantha`). Identifiers are the only way to disambiguate voices that share a name across languages or quality tiers.
 
+For the `siri` engine, use the full id returned by
+`GET /v1/audio/voices/all` (for example
+`com.apple.siri.tts.voice.en_US.nora.natural.premium`).
+
